This is dedicated to those people who nominated the scroll of fire as
a completely useless object in the useless object thread that was
running a few months ago.

In the process of being fondled by a few nurses, the untimely appearance
of various monsters led to me ending up naked and trapped in a corridor,
with a nurse on one side and a monster on the other:

                        |..
	     #####M@@###-.. 
			|..

I can't wield my weapon or put on any armor, or my nurse will make very
short work of me. I'm losing hit points faster than she is replacing
them, and without being able to use a weapon I'll be dead meat long
before the monster. I haven't got teleport or any good wands.
BUT....
       I did have in my inventory two scrolls of fire which I hadn't
got around to #dipping yet. I read them, and the resulting fireballs
which engulfed us killed the monster, didn't upset the nurse, and the
damage done to me was quickly repaired by my friendly assistant. I could 
then escape up the corridor, put on my speed boots and armour, despatch
the remaining baddies, and resume my dangerous liaison.

